  "script": "With 627 horsepower, it's the lightest, most powerful M5 ever built. This is the 2022 BMW M5 CS. Launched in 2022, the M5 CS used carbon fiber to shed 256 pounds over the standard M5. Under the hood is a 4.4-liter turbocharged V8 that redlines at 7,200 rpm and produces 553 lb-ft of torque. It features an all-wheel-drive system with rear-wheel drive capabilities for a dynamic driving experience. Inside, M carbon bucket seats and a 16-speaker Harman/Kardon stereo elevate the experience. Originally priced around $142,000, these now go for about $172,233 today, boasting a zero to sixty time of just 2.8 seconds. Would you choose this cutting-edge sedan over its less agile siblings?",
